{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workflows are closures. Every invocation runs the handler from the top. Replay short-circuits past completed work by reading the event log."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-log","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The log"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Append-only. Optimistic-CAS on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expectedNextIndex"},{"type":"text","value":". Stored via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore.appendEvent(runId, index, event)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checkpoint events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — replay reads these to skip work:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FAILED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SIGNAL_RESOLVED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"APPROVAL_RESOLVED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NOW_RECORDED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UUID_RECORDED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERRORED"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Coordination events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — persisted so hosts and resume calls can identify the pending wait:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SIGNAL_AWAITED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"APPROVAL_REQUESTED"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability-only events"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — emit-only, not persisted:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_STARTED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STATE_DELTA"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" (from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.emit"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-replay-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How replay works"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.step('id', fn)"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Walk the log for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FAILED"},{"type":"text","value":" with this "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Found → return the recorded result (or rethrow the recorded error). "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn"},{"type":"text","value":" is NOT called."}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not found → run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn"},{"type":"text","value":", append "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STEP_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":", return."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same algorithm for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitForEvent"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approve"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"now"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uuid"},{"type":"text","value":": replay first\nmatches the operation's durable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stepId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.step(id, ...)"},{"type":"text","value":" uses its first\nargument. Other primitives accept "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" in their options and otherwise use a\ngenerated positional internal ID."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"determinism-contract","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Determinism contract"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The handler "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"must"}]},{"type":"text","value":" reach the same primitives in the same order on every replay:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Determinism violations:\nconst t = Date.now()                 // use ctx.now()\nconst id = Math.random()             // use ctx.uuid()\nif (await fetchFlag()) { ... }       // wrap the fetch in ctx.step()\n\n// Safe:\nconst t = await ctx.now({ id: 'started-at' })\nconst id = await ctx.uuid({ id: 'correlation-id' })\nconst flag = await ctx.step('flag', fetchFlag)\nif (flag) { ... }","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State mutations re-run on replay. They're reapplied deterministically because they depend only on replayed step results."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pause-and-resume","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pause and resume"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run pauses when the handler reaches:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.approve"},{"type":"text","value":" with no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"APPROVAL_RESOLVED"},{"type":"text","value":" in the log"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.waitForEvent(name)"},{"type":"text","value":" with no matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SIGNAL_RESOLVED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.sleep"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.sleepUntil"},{"type":"text","value":" (internally a signal-wait on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__timer"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine writes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunState.status = 'paused'"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaiting[]"},{"type":"text","value":" populated, also\nfilling the current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitingFor"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingApproval"},{"type":"text","value":" projection fields, ends the\nevent stream, and returns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resume:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"runWorkflow({\n  workflow,\n  runId,\n  runStore,\n  // pick one:\n  approval:        { approvalId, approved, feedback? },\n  signalDelivery:  { signalId, stepId?, name, payload },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine appends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"APPROVAL_RESOLVED"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SIGNAL_RESOLVED"},{"type":"text","value":" to the log, re-runs the handler from the top, and replay carries through to the next primitive after the pause."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"idempotency-and-lost-races","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Idempotency and lost races"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every signal delivery carries a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signalId"},{"type":"text","value":". If the waited operation has an\nexplicit ID, pass it back as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signalDelivery.stepId"},{"type":"text","value":". Two deliveries for the\nsame waiting operation:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signalId"}]},{"type":"text","value":" → idempotent. The engine no-ops and returns success."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Different "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signalId"}]},{"type":"text","value":" → the loser sees "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERRORED { code: 'signal_lost' }"},{"type":"text","value":". The winner's payload is what the workflow sees."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this for safe webhook retries: pick a stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signalId"},{"type":"text","value":" per webhook event."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"version-routing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version routing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When workflow code changes, declare a version and keep old code reachable:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const v2 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v2' })\n  .previousVersions([v1])        // v1 stays callable for in-flight v1 runs\n  .handler(async (ctx) => { /* v2 body */ })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On resume the engine reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunState.workflowVersion"},{"type":"text","value":" and routes to the matching definition. Drop a version from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previousVersions"},{"type":"text","value":" only after all runs at that version have terminated."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mismatched version with nothing in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previousVersions"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERRORED { code: 'workflow_version_mismatch' }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attach-read-only-subscribe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach (read-only subscribe)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second subscriber (browser refresh, mobile reconnect) reads current state without driving the run forward:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"runWorkflow({ workflow, runId, runStore, attach: true })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Engine emits: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" → replay of the log → terminal event ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_ERRORED"},{"type":"text","value":", or pause info), then ends."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"webhook-execution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Webhook execution"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Durable-Streams-style stateless invocations:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { handleWorkflowWebhook } from '@tanstack/workflow-core'\n\nawait handleWorkflowWebhook({\n  workflow,\n  runStore,\n  payload: { runId, signalDelivery, approval },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same engine. One invocation drives the run to its next pause or completion. The HTTP handler returns; the durable stream / queue handles wake-ups."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cleanup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Terminal runs remain in the store so attach calls and webhook retries can read the final log. Stores decide their retention policy; the in-memory store expires non-paused runs after its TTL (1h default). Hosts can still call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore.deleteRun(runId, reason)"},{"type":"text","value":" when they want immediate cleanup."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-log-contains-end-to-end","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the log contains, end to end"}]},{"type":"code","value":"[\n  // RUN_STARTED — emit only, not in the persisted log\n  STEP_FINISHED   { stepId: 'fetch-user', result: { id: 'u-1', tier: 'pro' } },\n  NOW_RECORDED    { stepId: '__now-0', value: 1737499200000 },\n  SIGNAL_AWAITED  { stepId: 'payment-webhook', name: 'payment', deadline: ... },\n  SIGNAL_RESOLVED { stepId: 'payment-webhook', name: 'payment', signalId: 'evt-1', payload: { ... } },\n  APPROVAL_REQUESTED { stepId: 'review', approvalId: 'a-1', title: 'Continue?' },\n  APPROVAL_RESOLVED  { stepId: 'review', approvalId: 'a-1', approved: true },\n  STEP_FINISHED   { stepId: 'finalize', result: { ok: true } },\n  RUN_FINISHED    { runId, output: { ok: true } },\n]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replay walks this; observers tail it."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-log","text":"The log","level":2},{"id":"how-replay-works","text":"How replay works","level":2},{"id":"determinism-contract","text":"Determinism contract","level":2},{"id":"pause-and-resume","text":"Pause and resume","level":2},{"id":"idempotency-and-lost-races","text":"Idempotency and lost races","level":2},{"id":"version-routing","text":"Version routing","level":2},{"id":"attach-read-only-subscribe","text":"Attach (read-only subscribe)","level":2},{"id":"webhook-execution","text":"Webhook execution","level":2},{"id":"cleanup","text":"Cleanup","level":2},{"id":"what-the-log-contains-end-to-end","text":"What the log contains, end to end","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWorkflows are closures. Every invocation runs the handler from the top. Replay short-circuits past completed work by reading the event log.\n\n## The log\n\nAppend-only. Optimistic-CAS on `expectedNextIndex`. Stored via `RunStore.appendEvent(runId, index, event)`.\n\n**Checkpoint events** — replay reads these to skip work:\n- `STEP_FINISHED` / `STEP_FAILED`\n- `SIGNAL_RESOLVED` / `APPROVAL_RESOLVED`\n- `NOW_RECORDED` / `UUID_RECORDED`\n- `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERRORED`\n\n**Coordination events** — persisted so hosts and resume calls can identify the pending wait:\n- `SIGNAL_AWAITED`\n- `APPROVAL_REQUESTED`\n\n**Observability-only events** — emit-only, not persisted:\n- `RUN_STARTED`, `STEP_STARTED`\n- `STATE_DELTA`\n- `CUSTOM` (from `ctx.emit`)\n\n## How replay works\n\nFor each `ctx.step('id', fn)`:\n1. Walk the log for `STEP_FINISHED` / `STEP_FAILED` with this `id`.\n2. Found → return the recorded result (or rethrow the recorded error). **`fn` is NOT called.**\n3. Not found → run `fn`, append `STEP_FINISHED`, return.\n\nSame algorithm for `waitForEvent`, `approve`, `now`, and `uuid`: replay first\nmatches the operation's durable `stepId`. `ctx.step(id, ...)` uses its first\nargument. Other primitives accept `id` in their options and otherwise use a\ngenerated positional internal ID.\n\n## Determinism contract\n\nThe handler **must** reach the same primitives in the same order on every replay:\n\n```ts\n// Determinism violations:\nconst t = Date.now()                 // use ctx.now()\nconst id = Math.random()             // use ctx.uuid()\nif (await fetchFlag()) { ... }       // wrap the fetch in ctx.step()\n\n// Safe:\nconst t = await ctx.now({ id: 'started-at' })\nconst id = await ctx.uuid({ id: 'correlation-id' })\nconst flag = await ctx.step('flag', fetchFlag)\nif (flag) { ... }\n```\n\nState mutations re-run on replay. They're reapplied deterministically because they depend only on replayed step results.\n\n## Pause and resume\n\nRun pauses when the handler reaches:\n- `ctx.approve` with no `APPROVAL_RESOLVED` in the log\n- `ctx.waitForEvent(name)` with no matching `SIGNAL_RESOLVED`\n- `ctx.sleep` / `ctx.sleepUntil` (internally a signal-wait on `__timer`)\n\nThe engine writes `RunState.status = 'paused'` with `awaiting[]` populated, also\nfilling the current `waitingFor` / `pendingApproval` projection fields, ends the\nevent stream, and returns.\n\nResume:\n\n```ts\nrunWorkflow({\n  workflow,\n  runId,\n  runStore,\n  // pick one:\n  approval:        { approvalId, approved, feedback? },\n  signalDelivery:  { signalId, stepId?, name, payload },\n})\n```\n\nThe engine appends `APPROVAL_RESOLVED` or `SIGNAL_RESOLVED` to the log, re-runs the handler from the top, and replay carries through to the next primitive after the pause.\n\n## Idempotency and lost races\n\nEvery signal delivery carries a `signalId`. If the waited operation has an\nexplicit ID, pass it back as `signalDelivery.stepId`. Two deliveries for the\nsame waiting operation:\n\n- **Same `signalId`** → idempotent. The engine no-ops and returns success.\n- **Different `signalId`** → the loser sees `RUN_ERRORED { code: 'signal_lost' }`. The winner's payload is what the workflow sees.\n\nUse this for safe webhook retries: pick a stable `signalId` per webhook event.\n\n## Version routing\n\nWhen workflow code changes, declare a version and keep old code reachable:\n\n```ts\nconst v2 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v2' })\n  .previousVersions([v1])        // v1 stays callable for in-flight v1 runs\n  .handler(async (ctx) => { /* v2 body */ })\n```\n\nOn resume the engine reads `RunState.workflowVersion` and routes to the matching definition. Drop a version from `previousVersions` only after all runs at that version have terminated.\n\nMismatched version with nothing in `previousVersions` → `RUN_ERRORED { code: 'workflow_version_mismatch' }`.\n\n## Attach (read-only subscribe)\n\nA second subscriber (browser refresh, mobile reconnect) reads current state without driving the run forward:\n\n```ts\nrunWorkflow({ workflow, runId, runStore, attach: true })\n```\n\nEngine emits: `RUN_STARTED` → replay of the log → terminal event (`RUN_FINISHED`, `RUN_ERRORED`, or pause info), then ends.\n\n## Webhook execution\n\nFor Durable-Streams-style stateless invocations:\n\n```ts\nimport { handleWorkflowWebhook } from '@tanstack/workflow-core'\n\nawait handleWorkflowWebhook({\n  workflow,\n  runStore,\n  payload: { runId, signalDelivery, approval },\n})\n```\n\nSame engine. One invocation drives the run to its next pause or completion. The HTTP handler returns; the durable stream / queue handles wake-ups.\n\n## Cleanup\n\nTerminal runs remain in the store so attach calls and webhook retries can read the final log. Stores decide their retention policy; the in-memory store expires non-paused runs after its TTL (1h default). Hosts can still call `RunStore.deleteRun(runId, reason)` when they want immediate cleanup.\n\n## What the log contains, end to end\n\n```\n[\n  // RUN_STARTED — emit only, not in the persisted log\n  STEP_FINISHED   { stepId: 'fetch-user', result: { id: 'u-1', tier: 'pro' } },\n  NOW_RECORDED    { stepId: '__now-0', value: 1737499200000 },\n  SIGNAL_AWAITED  { stepId: 'payment-webhook', name: 'payment', deadline: ... },\n  SIGNAL_RESOLVED { stepId: 'payment-webhook', name: 'payment', signalId: 'evt-1', payload: { ... } },\n  APPROVAL_REQUESTED { stepId: 'review', approvalId: 'a-1', title: 'Continue?' },\n  APPROVAL_RESOLVED  { stepId: 'review', approvalId: 'a-1', approved: true },\n  STEP_FINISHED   { stepId: 'finalize', result: { ok: true } },\n  RUN_FINISHED    { runId, output: { ok: true } },\n]\n```\n\nReplay walks this; observers tail it.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: replay-and-resume\ntitle: Replay and Resume\n---\n\nWorkflows are closures. Every invocation runs the handler from the top. Replay short-circuits past completed work by reading the event log.\n\n## The log\n\nAppend-only. Optimistic-CAS on `expectedNextIndex`. Stored via `RunStore.appendEvent(runId, index, event)`.\n\n**Checkpoint events** — replay reads these to skip work:\n- `STEP_FINISHED` / `STEP_FAILED`\n- `SIGNAL_RESOLVED` / `APPROVAL_RESOLVED`\n- `NOW_RECORDED` / `UUID_RECORDED`\n- `RUN_FINISHED` / `RUN_ERRORED`\n\n**Coordination events** — persisted so hosts and resume calls can identify the pending wait:\n- `SIGNAL_AWAITED`\n- `APPROVAL_REQUESTED`\n\n**Observability-only events** — emit-only, not persisted:\n- `RUN_STARTED`, `STEP_STARTED`\n- `STATE_DELTA`\n- `CUSTOM` (from `ctx.emit`)\n\n## How replay works\n\nFor each `ctx.step('id', fn)`:\n1. Walk the log for `STEP_FINISHED` / `STEP_FAILED` with this `id`.\n2. Found → return the recorded result (or rethrow the recorded error). **`fn` is NOT called.**\n3. Not found → run `fn`, append `STEP_FINISHED`, return.\n\nSame algorithm for `waitForEvent`, `approve`, `now`, and `uuid`: replay first\nmatches the operation's durable `stepId`. `ctx.step(id, ...)` uses its first\nargument. Other primitives accept `id` in their options and otherwise use a\ngenerated positional internal ID.\n\n## Determinism contract\n\nThe handler **must** reach the same primitives in the same order on every replay:\n\n```ts\n// Determinism violations:\nconst t = Date.now()                 // use ctx.now()\nconst id = Math.random()             // use ctx.uuid()\nif (await fetchFlag()) { ... }       // wrap the fetch in ctx.step()\n\n// Safe:\nconst t = await ctx.now({ id: 'started-at' })\nconst id = await ctx.uuid({ id: 'correlation-id' })\nconst flag = await ctx.step('flag', fetchFlag)\nif (flag) { ... }\n```\n\nState mutations re-run on replay. They're reapplied deterministically because they depend only on replayed step results.\n\n## Pause and resume\n\nRun pauses when the handler reaches:\n- `ctx.approve` with no `APPROVAL_RESOLVED` in the log\n- `ctx.waitForEvent(name)` with no matching `SIGNAL_RESOLVED`\n- `ctx.sleep` / `ctx.sleepUntil` (internally a signal-wait on `__timer`)\n\nThe engine writes `RunState.status = 'paused'` with `awaiting[]` populated, also\nfilling the current `waitingFor` / `pendingApproval` projection fields, ends the\nevent stream, and returns.\n\nResume:\n\n```ts\nrunWorkflow({\n  workflow,\n  runId,\n  runStore,\n  // pick one:\n  approval:        { approvalId, approved, feedback? },\n  signalDelivery:  { signalId, stepId?, name, payload },\n})\n```\n\nThe engine appends `APPROVAL_RESOLVED` or `SIGNAL_RESOLVED` to the log, re-runs the handler from the top, and replay carries through to the next primitive after the pause.\n\n## Idempotency and lost races\n\nEvery signal delivery carries a `signalId`. If the waited operation has an\nexplicit ID, pass it back as `signalDelivery.stepId`. Two deliveries for the\nsame waiting operation:\n\n- **Same `signalId`** → idempotent. The engine no-ops and returns success.\n- **Different `signalId`** → the loser sees `RUN_ERRORED { code: 'signal_lost' }`. The winner's payload is what the workflow sees.\n\nUse this for safe webhook retries: pick a stable `signalId` per webhook event.\n\n## Version routing\n\nWhen workflow code changes, declare a version and keep old code reachable:\n\n```ts\nconst v2 = createWorkflow({ id: 'pipeline', version: 'v2' })\n  .previousVersions([v1])        // v1 stays callable for in-flight v1 runs\n  .handler(async (ctx) => { /* v2 body */ })\n```\n\nOn resume the engine reads `RunState.workflowVersion` and routes to the matching definition. Drop a version from `previousVersions` only after all runs at that version have terminated.\n\nMismatched version with nothing in `previousVersions` → `RUN_ERRORED { code: 'workflow_version_mismatch' }`.\n\n## Attach (read-only subscribe)\n\nA second subscriber (browser refresh, mobile reconnect) reads current state without driving the run forward:\n\n```ts\nrunWorkflow({ workflow, runId, runStore, attach: true })\n```\n\nEngine emits: `RUN_STARTED` → replay of the log → terminal event (`RUN_FINISHED`, `RUN_ERRORED`, or pause info), then ends.\n\n## Webhook execution\n\nFor Durable-Streams-style stateless invocations:\n\n```ts\nimport { handleWorkflowWebhook } from '@tanstack/workflow-core'\n\nawait handleWorkflowWebhook({\n  workflow,\n  runStore,\n  payload: { runId, signalDelivery, approval },\n})\n```\n\nSame engine. One invocation drives the run to its next pause or completion. The HTTP handler returns; the durable stream / queue handles wake-ups.\n\n## Cleanup\n\nTerminal runs remain in the store so attach calls and webhook retries can read the final log. Stores decide their retention policy; the in-memory store expires non-paused runs after its TTL (1h default). Hosts can still call `RunStore.deleteRun(runId, reason)` when they want immediate cleanup.\n\n## What the log contains, end to end\n\n```\n[\n  // RUN_STARTED — emit only, not in the persisted log\n  STEP_FINISHED   { stepId: 'fetch-user', result: { id: 'u-1', tier: 'pro' } },\n  NOW_RECORDED    { stepId: '__now-0', value: 1737499200000 },\n  SIGNAL_AWAITED  { stepId: 'payment-webhook', name: 'payment', deadline: ... },\n  SIGNAL_RESOLVED { stepId: 'payment-webhook', name: 'payment', signalId: 'evt-1', payload: { ... } },\n  APPROVAL_REQUESTED { stepId: 'review', approvalId: 'a-1', title: 'Continue?' },\n  APPROVAL_RESOLVED  { stepId: 'review', approvalId: 'a-1', approved: true },\n  STEP_FINISHED   { stepId: 'finalize', result: { ok: true } },\n  RUN_FINISHED    { runId, output: { ok: true } },\n]\n```\n\nReplay walks this; observers tail it.\n"}
